# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for PlatformService.
#
# These match known-benign, out-of-our-control races reported inside library
# internals: OpenSSL 3.x's lock-free algorithm-fetch cache, and glibc's
# pthread_create stack-cache reuse. Neither has ever shown a single frame
# from this project's own code -- confirmed with Helgrind during development
# of the phase-2 net/tls/threadpool/conn/server modules, where both patterns
# showed up entirely inside libcrypto.so and glibc's pthread implementation.
#
# `make test SANFLAGS="-fsanitize=thread"` is currently clean with zero
# findings even without these; they're kept as a documented safety net,
# since sanitizer output can depend on thread scheduling and CI runner load.

race:libcrypto
race:OSSL_LIB_CTX_get0_global_default
race:EVP_KEM_fetch
race:allocate_stack
race:get_cached_stack
race:_dl_allocate_tls
